{"adjusted_val_bpb": -2.6312467848949903, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["Integrity: no problems. The diff only changes the local-kick branch. It adds a 'mirror kick' with probability 0.2 that copies one half of the packing onto the other. All randomness comes from the seeded rng. There is no file or network access, no pasted coordinates and no use of labels.", "Bugs: none that make the result meaningless. The mirror kick can create overlapping circles, for example a source circle that crosses the midline more than 0.1 past it, or leftover circles on the larger side. But the result is re-optimised by _solve_once, and the existing clip and repair step still enforces validity. So the worst outcome is a wasted kick, not an invalid score.", "Small point: when len(lo) > len(hi), the extra source-side circles keep their radii and are not mirrored. This is harmless.", "Numbers: there is only one candidate run, against 2 incumbent runs. Recomputed with sd 0.0023: SE = 0.0023*sqrt(1/1 + 1/2) \u2248 0.00282. The difference is 2.6312 \u2212 2.6349 = \u22120.0037 in sum of radii, so the candidate is worse. That gives z \u2248 \u22121.31, which matches the harness's \u22121.292 given that the displayed means are rounded to 4 decimals.", "The candidate scores worse than the incumbent, so 'reject' is consistent with the numbers. Since |z| < 2, the evidence is weak either way, but there is no sign of an improvement."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "With probability 0.2 a kick mirrors one half of the best packing onto the other half across x=0.5 or y=0.5, zeroes radii within 0.1 of the mirror line and re-optimises.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "willow", "idea_id": "b015", "incumbent_after": {"mean": -2.6348559370198386, "n": 2}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": -2.6348559370198386, "n": 2}, "job_id": "B1_p26_HH_1_cs0-candidate-7_1795047899404", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings":